{
  "id": "COMPOUND:30124 - PROTEIN:5852",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between 7-O-Methylmangiferin and BT-474, with the compound acting as a target for multiple downstream molecules. The evidence indicates that 7-O-Methylmangiferin interacts with MIP, which in turn is targeted by both 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and Maplexin A. These two compounds are both implicated in targeting BT-474, a breast cancer cell line, suggesting a potential role for 7-O-Methylmangiferin in modulating the activity of these molecules. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which 7-O-Methylmangiferin may influence BT-474 through the activation or inhibition of key molecular targets. The recurring involvement of MIP and the shared target of multiple compounds further supports the idea that 7-O-Methylmangiferin may exert its biological effects through a network of molecular interactions, potentially involving the regulation of cellular processes critical to cancer progression.",
